   "subject": "Poisson Likelihood with non-integer response",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<br><br>Is it possible to fit a Poisson model to non-integer data in INLA (similar to what the quasipoisson family does in glm)?<br><br>Thanks in advance,<br><br>Abdollah<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sA0lSCN-BwAJ",
   "from": "INLA help",
   "author": "3eab71733027a24a",
   "date": "2016-07-23T12:46:13Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Poisson Likelihood with non-integer response",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Sat, 2016-07-23 at 05:37 -0700, AJ wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hello,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Is it possible to fit a Poisson model to non-integer data in INLA\r<br>&gt; (similar to what the quasipoisson family does in glm)?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "no. \r<br>\r<br>what would the expression for that likelihood be in that case?\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Håvard Rue\r<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
